	[2664]={
		encounterID=2664,
		instanceID=1301,
		order=2,
		name="Bael'Gar",
		lore="The monstrous molten giant Bael'Gar lumbers across the Dark Iron Highway, a stunning feat of dwarven engineering carved into Blackrock Depths. Ragnaros pulled the giant from the heart of the Firelands to guard a massive sealed door at one end of the highway. According to legend, only the Firelord and the Dark Iron clan's highest-ranking members know what lies beyond the mysterious gate.",
		dungeonEncounterID=3044,
		uiMapID=2363,
		pin={x=0.2514,y=0.5348},
		difficultyIDs={14,15,17},
		npcIDs={226303},
		displayIDs={120759,122126},
		loot={
			{itemID=231409,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231411,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231447,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231458,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231408,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231461,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231410,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231462,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231463,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=30732,title="Overview",body="Bael'Gar's |cFF2959D3|Hspell:462974|h[Giant Strike]|h|r inflicts enormous damage in a cone in front of him with every swing. Damage is split between players struck.\n\n|cFF2959D3|Hspell:463890|h[Rockfall]|h|r causes large boulders and small rocks to fall from the ceiling that players must avoid. Players will need to seek cover when Bael'Gar casts |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463143|h[Molten Furnace]|h|r. Any boulders that remain when Bael'Gar casts |cFF2959D3|Hspell:462972|h[Shatter]|h|r will inflict significant additional damage to the entire raid.\n\nWhenever a boulder is destroyed, several Spawns of Bael'Gar are created. When a Spawn of Bael'Gar is killed, its |cFF2959D3|Hspell:462968|h[Molten Heart]|h|r inflicts damage over time to a random player."},
			{id=30733,title="Tanks",body="$bullet; Tanks will need to split the damage of |cFF2959D3|Hspell:462974|h[Giant Strike]|h|r in order to survive.\n$bullet; The large boulders created by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463890|h[Rockfall]|h|r inflict higher damage the nearer players are to the point of impact.\n$bullet; Any boulders that remain when Bael'Gar casts |cFF2959D3|Hspell:462972|h[Shatter]|h|r have the potential to make its damage lethal.\n$bullet; When a boulder is destroyed several Spawns of Bael'Gar will be created and attack nearby players."},
			{id=30734,title="Damage Dealers",body="$bullet; The large boulders created by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463890|h[Rockfall]|h|r inflict higher damage the nearer players are to the point of impact.\n$bullet; |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463143|h[Molten Furnace]|h|r inflicts lethal damage to players that are not behind cover.\n$bullet; Any boulders that remain when Bael'Gar casts |cFF2959D3|Hspell:462972|h[Shatter]|h|r have the potential to make its damage lethal.\n$bullet; When a boulder is destroyed several Spawns of Bael'Gar will be created and attack nearby players."},
			{id=30735,title="Healers",body="$bullet; Tanks will need to split the damage of |cFF2959D3|Hspell:462974|h[Giant Strike]|h|r in order to survive.\n$bullet; The large boulders created by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463890|h[Rockfall]|h|r inflict higher damage the nearer players are to the point of impact.\n$bullet; |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463143|h[Molten Furnace]|h|r inflicts lethal damage to players that are not behind cover.\n$bullet; Any boulders that remain when Bael'Gar casts |cFF2959D3|Hspell:462972|h[Shatter]|h|r have the potential to make its damage lethal.\n$bullet; When Spawns of Bael'Gar are killed they will deal damage over time to a random player with |cFF2959D3|Hspell:462968|h[Molten Heart]|h|r."},
			{id=30736,title="Section 5"},
			{id=30737,title="Section 6"},
			{id=30947,title="Boulder",body="Boulders can be used to hide from Molten Furnace and release Spawns of Bael'Gar when destroyed."},
			{id=30740,title="Spawn of Bael'Gar"},
			{id=30946,title="Section 10"},
			{id=30948,title="Section 12"},
			{id=30738,title="Section 7"},
			{id=30739,title="Section 8"},
		},
	},
	[2665]={
		encounterID=2665,
		instanceID=1301,
		order=3,
		name="Lord Incendius",
		lore="Baron Geddon taught Incendius to harness his destructive powers, but the baron never expected his protege to grow so lethally efficient. Increasingly wary that Incendius might usurp him, Geddon sent the blazing elemental out of the Molten Core to guard the Dark Iron dwarves' fabled Black Anvil.",
		dungeonEncounterID=3043,
		uiMapID=2363,
		pin={x=0.4626,y=0.4639},
		difficultyIDs={14,15,17},
		npcIDs={226304},
		displayIDs={120760,122227},
		loot={
			{itemID=231406,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231467,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231404,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231468,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231405,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231464,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=231407,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=30741,title="Overview",body="Lord Incendius summons powerful Flame Geysers that will inflict deadly damage until they are brought under control. Even in defeat, a |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463486|h[Flame Geyser]|h|r casts |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463472|h[Dying Flare]|h|r which can hurl players off the bridge and inflict high damage.\n\nLord Incendius will attempt to force players off the bridge with |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463495|h[Scorching Wind]|h|r. Tanks will need to work together to prevent |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463499|h[Blowback]|h|r from throwing them off the bridge.\n\nFlame Geysers that remain when Lord Incendius casts |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463495|h[Scorching Wind]|h|r may become extremely deadly."},
			{id=30742,title="Tanks",body="$bullet; Flame Geysers become more deadly the longer they are left alive. Each cast of |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463471|h[Blaze]|h|r becomes successively faster.\n$bullet; When a Flame Geyser is defeated, players must split the damage caused by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463472|h[Dying Flare]|h|r.\n$bullet; Taunt Lord Incendius to prevent the other tank from being pushed off the bridge by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463499|h[Blowback]|h|r.\n$bullet; Be wary of being pushed off the bridge by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463472|h[Dying Flare]|h|r or |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463495|h[Scorching Wind]|h|r."},
			{id=30743,title="Damage Dealers",body="$bullet; Flame Geysers become more deadly the longer they are left alive. Each cast of |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463471|h[Blaze]|h|r becomes successively faster.\n$bullet; When a Flame Geyser is defeated, players must split the damage caused by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463472|h[Dying Flare]|h|r.\n$bullet; Be wary of being pushed off the bridge by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463472|h[Dying Flare]|h|r or |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463495|h[Scorching Wind]|h|r."},
			{id=30744,title="Healers",body="$bullet; |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463503|h[Consumptive Flames]|h|r inflicts a short burst of high damage.\n$bullet; Flame Geysers have the potential to inflict high damage to the entire raid until they are brought under control and defeated.\n$bullet; It will be difficult to stop and cast during |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463495|h[Scorching Wind]|h|r.\n$bullet; Be wary of being pushed off the bridge by |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463472|h[Dying Flare]|h|r or |cFF2959D3|Hspell:463495|h[Scorching Wind]|h|r."},
			{id=30745,title="Section 10"},
			{id=30746,title="Section 9"},
